  "metric": "Rank of the observed largest power among 200 character-count label shuffles, at one probe window.",
  "notes": "The largest power ranges over whole cycle counts of two or more only, each with a period of 4 or more in the labelling's own units. That is this rung's one committed change. The one-cycle bin is computed and saved in every spectrum, observed and shuffled alike, and can never be the statistic. After the fixed degree-2 detrend that bin measures the profile's leftover curvature, so a single smooth drop across a window lands there, and such a drop is not a repeating pattern. The one-cycle power above is the quantity that restriction excludes, recorded so it can be read rather than guessed. Shuffling permutes the character-count labels inside each held-out document, so every label keeps exactly the same number of positions. With 200 draws the finest share this can resolve is about 0.5 percent. The seed values above all derive from the one committed base seed, 0. Every draw's whole spectrum is in the named file beside this record, and every line there names the minimum number of cycles it was computed under. The average vectors of the observed labelling are saved too. The average vectors of each draw are not saved, as the previous rung's gate record settles. The counts of directions above are recorded and gate nothing at this rung. If the floor gate recorded in these values failed, this record is void as evidence about the model, and is an instrument fault only. A further run of this script on the same box is a rerun of the same instrument, not a replication.",
